            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "29764939"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Catalyzes the dehalogenation of halotyrosines such as 3-bromo-L-tyrosine, 3-chloro-L-tyrosine, 3-iodo-L-tyrosine and 3,5-diiodo-L-tyrosine (PubMed:27643701). Activity towards 3-fluoro-L-tyrosine is weak (PubMed:27643701). Important for male and female fertility (PubMed:29764939). May be involved in maintaining the viability of sperm, both during development in the testes and storage in the female spermatheca (PubMed:29764939)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
    },
